From 759ce55d9cb575c1f45fcade765c50b6332f9443 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 19:11:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07246/11362] [outer-loop] redirect retired ARC floor to
 generalization research (operator-chosen)

Follow-up to the ARC public-game-solving floor retirement (commit
56d91abec). Asked the operator what should fill the reserved ARC slot now
that all 25 public games are cleared; answer: "Redirect to generalization
research" -- test/improve how well accumulated per-game methods transfer to
games the live agent hasn't been specifically hand-tuned for, rather than
submission packaging or dropping the floor entirely.

Added CLAUDE.md "ARC-AGI-3 Generalization-Testing Floor" (new rule,
supersedes the retired public-solving floor at the same >=1-slot/milestone
cadence through November 2026). Three task classes count: held-out/
leave-one-game-out live-path measurement (disable a GameAdapter, run the
real E3AgentPolicy/scored path, see how far reusable scaffolding alone
gets), arc_solver_kit.py reusable-primitive hardening, or cross-game
gotcha-mining into a shared primitive.

Implemented the mechanical side for real (not just documented as future
work): scripts/arc_levelup_guarantee_lint.py gained
_is_generalization_attempt()/count_generalization_attempts(), wired into
research_conductor.py's activation guard as a WARN-only check (never
refuses activation -- the detection heuristic is new and unproven, and a
hard gate on a fuzzy match risks recreating the exact deadlock the original
floor's retirement was fixing). Fixed a real bug found while testing: the
registry-path default argument was bound at function-definition time, so a
test-time monkeypatch of the module path had no effect on the internal
call inside lint_roadmap; switched that call site to reference the module
global directly so it resolves live.

Added tests/python/test_arc_levelup_guarantee_lint.py (17 tests, all
passing via --no-cov per this repo's own documented coverage-tooling
gotcha): registry-driven retirement detection (clear/not-clear/missing/
malformed), the original level-up-attempt detector, and the new
generalization-attempt detector including a dedicated test locking in the
ARC-scoping guard (generic ML "generalization" language with no ARC/game
mention must not false-positive this floor -- verified against a realistic
non-ARC prompt).

